{"tool_name":"nextgenmap","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"nextgenmap","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btt468"],"license":"MIT","summary":"NextGenMap is a flexible highly sensitive short read mapping tool that","home_url":"https://github.com/Cibiv/NextGenMap","keywords":["Genome","Genomics","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Polymorphism, Genetic","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"nextgenmap","home":"http://cibiv.github.io/NextGenMap/","license":"MIT","summary":"NextGenMap is a flexible highly sensitive short read mapping tool that handles much higher mismatch rates than comparable algorithms while still outperforming them in terms of runtime.","addition_date":"2021-05-26T21:15:21Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:21:02.297786Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:nextgenmap","credit":[{"email":"fritz.sedlazeck@univie.ac.at","name":"Fritz J. Sedlazeck","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"philipp.rescheneder@univie.ac.at","name":"Fritz J. Sedlazeck","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["FAQ"],"url":"https://github.com/Cibiv/NextGenMap/wiki/FAQ"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/Cibiv/NextGenMap/wiki"},{"type":["Installation instructions"],"url":"https://github.com/Cibiv/NextGenMap/wiki/Installation"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/Cibiv/NextGenMap/wiki/Documentation"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0525"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"},{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"}]}],"name":"NextGenMap","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btt468","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: When choosing a read mapper, one faces the trade off between speed and the ability to map reads in highly polymorphic regions. Here, we report NextGenMap, a fast and accurate read mapper, which reduces this dilemma. NextGenMap aligns reads reliably to a reference genome even when the sequence difference between target and reference genome is large, i.e. highly polymorphic genome. At the same time, NextGenMap outperforms current mapping methods with respect to runtime and to the number of correctly mapped reads. NextGenMap efficiently uses the available hardware by exploiting multi-core CPUs as well as graphic cards (GPUs), if available. In addition, NextGenMap handles automatically any read data independent of read length and sequencing technology. Availability: NextGenMap source code and documentation are available at: http://cibiv.github.io/NextGenMap/. \u00a9 2013 The Author 2013.","authors":[{"name":"Rescheneder P."},{"name":"Sedlazeck F.J."},{"name":"Von Haeseler A."}],"citationCount":282,"date":"2013-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"NextGenMap: Fast and accurate read mapping in highly polymorphic genomes"},"pmid":"23975764","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0081"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"NextGenMap","home":"https://bio.tools/nextgenmap","license":"MIT","summary":"NextGenMap is a flexible highly sensitive short read mapping tool that handles much higher mismatch rates than comparable algorithms while still outperforming them in terms of runtime.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:nextgenmap/cmd/cibiv.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"s